24kz|n|The act or result of stirring; agitation; tumult; bustle; noise or various movements. ; Public disturbance or commotion; tumultuous disorder; seditious uproar. ; Agitation of thoughts; conflicting passions.	N:28w6,35,2~28w6,35,2
24kz|v|To change the place of in any manner; to move. ; To disturb the relative position of the particles of, as of a liquid, by passing something through it; to agitate; as, to stir a pudding with a spoon. ; To bring into debate; to agitate; to moot. ; To incite to action; to arouse; to instigate; to prompt; to excite. ; To move; to change one's position. ; To be in motion; to be active or bustling; to exert or busy one's self. ; To become the object of notice; to be on foot. ; To rise, or be up, in the morning.	o:28w6,53,7~28w6,53,7	D:2dm8,25,2~2dm8,25,2
