24y7|n|Strained; drawn close; tight; as, a strict embrace; a strict ligature. ; Tense; not relaxed; as, a strict fiber. ; Exact; accurate; precise; rigorously nice; as, to keep strict watch; to pay strict attention. ; Governed or governing by exact rules; observing exact rules; severe; rigorous; as, very strict in observing the Sabbath. ; Rigidly; interpreted; exactly limited; confined; restricted; as, to understand words in a strict sense. ; Upright, or straight and narrow; -- said of the shape of the plants or their flower clusters.	a:1k3x,31,2;1qqa,10,6~1qqa,10,6;1k3x,31,2	V:yeo,19,3~yeo,19,3	N:1ck4,48,1;1xbe,36,20;vjf,31,3;25ld,22,1;1vj2,19,4;1xba,14,3;yeo,14,2;z1w,9,1;yd2,3,1;1p3i,2,3~1xbe,36,20;1vj2,19,4;1p3i,2,3;1xba,14,3;vjf,31,3;yeo,14,2;yd2,3,1;z1w,9,1;25ld,22,1;1ck4,48,1
