24zy|v|To make efforts; to use exertions; to endeavor with earnestness; to labor hard. ; To struggle in opposition; to be in contention or dispute; to contend; to contest; -- followed by against or with before the person or thing opposed; as, strive against temptation; strive for the truth. ; To vie; to compete; to be a rival.	o:29zz,50,7~29zz,50,7	s:2cy6,32,6;2oc,10,2~2cy6,32,6;2oc,10,2	d:2oc,38,14;24i6,11,4;1tu6,0,2~2oc,38,14;24i6,11,4;1tu6,0,2
