254t|n|To fill by crowding something into; to cram with something; to load to excess; as, to stuff a bedtick. ; To thrust or crowd; to press; to pack. ; To fill by being pressed or packed into. ; To fill with a seasoning composition of bread, meat, condiments, etc.; as, to stuff a turkey. ; To obstruct, as any of the organs; to affect with some obstruction in the organs of sense or respiration. ; To fill the skin of, for the purpose of preserving as a specimen; -- said of birds or other animals. ; To form or fashion by packing with the necessary material. ; To crowd with facts; to cram the mind of; sometimes, to crowd or fill with false or idle tales or fancies. ; To put fraudulent votes into (a ballot box).	a:wf5,70,4;2cv6,59,11;tf3,57,26;1gb4,57,15;gxj,54,55;266j,53,4;156a,52,8;19k,51,50;1yhi,49,5;pjj,47,12;hys,47,16;9g1,46,15;1n5j,46,4;16on,43,29;wd4,42,26~1jjn,23,433;1gv5,25,204;y7k,11,131;13f7,27,117;15tg,35,94;71j,41,81;25t7,6,67;1fiq,6,67;27vu,35,57;gxj,54,55;1kei,10,53;19k,51,50;1mx1,21,48;1iii,24,48;1tiv,32,45	v:293v,49,11;u7h,46,13;are,44,18;1cyi,42,4;1vam,40,9;eqe,40,4;9g1,39,9;sdi,39,7;yvl,36,2;9w5,36,10;2dkc,34,4;ka6,33,11;h1f,33,14;2a3l,32,6;srq,25,13~np0,17,86;19at,7,32;1ux3,11,31;19ao,12,30;xgz,3,22;1bj4,8,20;are,44,18;1tst,7,16;15tg,10,16;h1f,33,14;1ybk,5,13;srq,25,13;u7h,46,13;13a,16,13;18an,7,11	V:zph,27,11;284w,26,7;1r4p,25,7;xgv,22,31;y4i,21,22;zpi,16,18;nsv,15,56;f88,11,9;15gp,10,15;27f1,10,12;y4x,9,44;2h15,9,25;1ux3,8,26;1fgr,6,4;f7f,6,12~nsv,15,56;y4x,9,44;xgv,22,31;1ux3,8,26;2h15,9,25;y4i,21,22;zpi,16,18;1s2n,0,17;15gp,10,15;f7f,6,12;27f1,10,12;zph,27,11;2h7e,1,11;f88,11,9;1gj8,2,7	n:96l,47,3;hu0,46,3;1yna,37,4;lbv,32,7;8fy,31,2;196,30,6;p30,28,10;tf3,26,3;hys,22,3;2dwo,20,5;6bg,19,2;1ibe,16,4;1gg6,13,1;9w5,12,2;1hm7,12,4~97,3,137;2784,7,35;1cd7,12,32;2bpv,8,16;2dwb,7,16;19om,1,13;1sud,5,12;18fe,5,11;1noz,5,10;p30,28,10;28qy,5,8;lbv,32,7;196,30,6;lci,11,6;2dwo,20,5	N:242m,10,5;zpi,9,11;1ipe,5,12~1ipe,5,12;zpi,9,11;242m,10,5
